{"title":"2008 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 8","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_OmegaLearn\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by OmegaLearn</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_8&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>What is the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Volume\" title=\"Volume\">volume</a> of a <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Cube\" title=\"Cube\">cube</a> whose <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Surface_area\" title=\"Surface area\">surface area</a> is twice that of a cube with volume 1? \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/4/b/94ba312fa1d2356496914af2d82008af1647235c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mathrm{(A)}\\ \\sqrt{2}\\qquad\\mathrm{(B)}\\ 2\\qquad\\mathrm{(C)}\\ 2\\sqrt{2}\\qquad\\mathrm{(D)}\\ 4\\qquad\\mathrm{(E)}\\ 8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"381\" height=\"21\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_8&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>A cube with volume <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> has a side of length <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/c/6/3c65bfc5db8bea84fcd769f69191c1c492e6718f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt[3]{1}=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"57\" height=\"18\" /> and thus a surface area of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/6/6063b4ed6dbc42e1608bacc42d3dd4812945e5e3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6 \\cdot 1^2=6$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"71\" height=\"15\" />. \n</p><p>A cube whose surface area is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/d/0/1d0c685d5d16fd64749b78fa5a4e4c36308a87b0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6\\cdot2=12$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"73\" height=\"13\" /> has a side of length <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/e/f/bef0f3eb69b7b933ef94b90846279b4f10902aae.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{\\frac{12}{6}}=\\sqrt{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -14px\" width=\"89\" height=\"43\" /> and a volume of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/4/0642fbc477356eb5e98c08504c2a6823c34363c7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(\\sqrt{2})^3=2\\sqrt{2}\\Rightarrow\\mathrm{(C)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"157\" height=\"21\" />.\n</p><p><br />\nAlternatively, we can use the fact that the surface area of a cube is directly proportional to the square of its side length. Therefore, if the surface area of a cube increases by a factor of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, its side length must increase by a factor of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/c/4/2c4dc1409208ff6a3039f4871d85c16763334983.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"26\" height=\"21\" />, meaning the new side length of the cube is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/6/e/c6e9b90f65708c881a714fe508e37fab90e74723.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1 * \\sqrt{2} = \\sqrt{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"99\" height=\"18\" />. So, its volume is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/5/c/35cfbc430d5c2cdbaf02004c6c4afb78f77419fc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$({\\sqrt{2}})^3 = 2\\sqrt{2} \\Rightarrow\\mathrm{(C)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"157\" height=\"21\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_OmegaLearn\">Video Solution by OmegaLearn</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_8&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by OmegaLearn\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/MOcX5BFbcwU?t=54\">https://youtu.be/MOcX5BFbcwU?t=54</a>\n</p><p>~ pi_is_3.14\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_8&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td styl